            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "amberwrites"
            },
            "reviewBody": "WOW! not to brag, but the changes i made to this recipe...i truly think they were the best mashed potatoes i have ever eaten. used about 7 medium russet potatoes, 1/2 cup sour cream, 1/2 cup heavy cream, 1 stick REAL butter, 1/2 cup parmesan cheese, 2 cloves garlic (mashed up), sea salt, and cracked black pepper. the KEY to making mashed potatoes creamy is NOT to over mix. set your mixer on about a \"4\" and mix until it resembles the texture of frosting. also, scrape the sides once about halfway thru the mixing. be careful not to fold too much when you scrape...all that GOOD mixing you are doing to FLUFF your potatoes will be wasted! total...i mix for about 1.5 minutes, scrape the sides, and mix for another 1.5-2.5 minutes."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sharon Robertson"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made a 1/5th of this for my husband and I and we both looved them...i boiled the potatoes in the microwave and used cream cheese/greek yogurt blend and Chobani sour cream/greek yogurt blend (and black truffle salt) for a healthier side dish.",
            "datePublished": "2020-02-11T04:54:27.367Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "DONNA"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great Recipe! Made a few changes. First of all raw garlic didn't appeal to me so i sauteed it first in some butter. The aroma is heavenly and i did cut down on the amount of parmesan and cream cheese and then added some milk for creaminess. Skipped the chives and salt and peppered well. Used a hand mixer and combined well ( a little chunky) and transferred to a greased foil pan to be reheated next day for Thanksgiving dinner. Garnished with some finely chopped parsley. Excellent!",
            "datePublished": "2017-11-22T16:57:02.200Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tiara Arzillo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I can't rate this recipe as is because I'm a tweaker and tweaking is what I do best! ;)\n\nMost of the time I go with the recipe as a base and build on it as I go.\n\nHeres what I did:\nBoiled about 3 lbs peeled and chopped potatoes in chicken broth with a little salt until tender. \n\nMashed with a stick of butter,\nA dollop of sour cream,\nA tsp or 2 of ranch dressing,\n1/2 cup 2% milk,\nA few slices of havarti cheese,\nAbout 1/4 cup of grated parm,\nTsp each of garlic and onion powder,\nsalt and parsley to taste. \n\nMashed it all up and mixed added the above till I got my desired taste. It was fantastic and even my 2 year old son who hates mashed potatoes LOVED it!. \n\nWill Def make again.",
            "datePublished": "2015-08-12T17:28:09.883Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Deena Kordt"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I prefer russet spuds, so used them several times now. Great results. Reduced parmesan to 3/4 cup, subbed in 1 cup sour cream; reduced cream cheese to 1/2 cup; subbed green onions for chives; added chicken bouillon to cooking water; boiled 4 whole large farmer's market garlic cloves with spuds &amp; mashed together; added warm milk/cream when mashing. Now a family favorite :)",
            "datePublished": "2015-10-14T12:25:02.963Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "april"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Always like to tweak recipes so..followed the advice of amber writes and added half cup sour cream and grated Parmesan, one stick softened butter, and almost 3/4 pint of heavy cream, all at room temperature so not to make them cold. Also boiled the potatoes with about 5 cloves of crushed garlic..probably the best mashed potatoes ever",
            "datePublished": "2015-11-26T13:51:22.150Z"
          },
